  "listens_rule": "RP-5 §4.4: a record's `listens` are windows of RP-7 §5's form. One holds with integer `every_s` of 1 or more, `at_s` below it and `length_s` from 1 to `every_s`; the others are ignored (`kept`, null when none holds or there is no `listens`: the gateway listens as `hours` says, and `open` is true with no change). A window opens `at_s` seconds after each multiple of `every_s` since the Unix epoch, for `length_s` seconds. At `now`, `open` says whether any window is open, and `changes` when that changes: when the stretch of windows open at `now`, following on or overlapping, ends; else when the next window opens. Windows that cover every moment never close: `changes` is null.",
